      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching appointment",
          "heading": "Jake White takes charge of Fiji after two decades away from internationals",
          "body": "Jake White is back coaching at international level after a 20-year gap, taking charge of Fiji with the 2007 World Cup on his résumé. \"I've not coached at international level for 20 years, but I was very excited today,\" he said after the Japan win. Eddie Jones is his technical adviser, and White's Europe-based players should be available for the three Nations Championship games against France, Ireland and Italy."
