      "edition": "Monday 26 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Honours revoked",
          "heading": "Stuart Hogg stripped of MBE after domestic abuse conviction, register confirms",
          "body": "Former Scotland captain Stuart Hogg has had his MBE removed, with the Cabinet Office's official register confirming the revocation was made in March after his domestic abuse conviction. Hogg, who won 100 caps for Scotland and toured three times with the British & Irish Lions, pleaded guilty to a domestic abuse charge involving his estranged wife, Gillian, and received a one-year community payback order in January 2025. The honour had been awarded in the 2024 New Year Honours for services to rugby."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland fly-half Sam Prendergast doubtful for Argentina Test with wrist injury",
          "body": "Wallabies start Declan Meredith at fly-half in Bledisloe Cup Test."
        }
      ]
    },
